# SKYNEX AI: REMOVE DEMO DATA AND IMPLEMENT THE REAL AI BRAND-GOVERNANCE ENGINE

## 1. YOUR ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, AI engineer, document-processing engineer, database architect, and QA engineer.

I already have an existing SkyNex AI website with a dashboard and these sections:

1. Review Content
2. Brand Knowledge
3. Review History
4. Recurring Issues

The interface exists, but it currently contains fictional demo brands, example rules, sample statistics, and simulated workflows.

Your task is to convert the EXISTING application into a functional, AI-powered brand-governance prototype that can be used by different organisations with their own brand guidelines, documents, product information, visual assets, and content.

**Do not build another frontend from scratch. Inspect the complete existing project and extend it. Preserve the existing design, routing, components, working backend integrations, and useful functionality.**

Do not stop after writing a plan. Implement the changes, run the available tests, fix errors, and report what genuinely works.

## 2. THE CORE PRODUCT REQUIREMENT

SkyNex AI must allow an organisation to upload its brand knowledge, extract individual rules using AI, review and approve those rules, and then evaluate submitted content against that organisation's approved knowledge.

The complete workflow must be:

Brand/workspace creation
→ Brand knowledge upload
→ Text and document extraction
→ AI rule interpretation
→ Candidate rule list
→ Human rule approval
→ Content submission
→ Content extraction and analysis
→ Approved-rule matching
→ Explainable findings and suggested corrections
→ Human review and decision
→ Saved review history
→ Recurring-issue and guideline-quality insights

Every step must work with actual application data. Do not use fake success messages, static results, hardcoded counts, or sample rules in production.

